{"availability":"available","full":"goepfert/noise_reduction","name":"noise_reduction","description":"Audio De-Noiser using a Convolutional Neural Network Architecture built with Tensorflow.js","category":"Education","language":"JavaScript","stars":22,"forks":3,"created":"2020-07-21T21:03:16Z","updated":"2023-06-07T20:13:59Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["audio","deep-neural-networks","demo","javascript","machine-learning","noise-reduction","speech","tensorflow","tensorflowjs"],"demo":"https://goepfert.github.io/noise_reduction/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.111Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.111Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.111Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.111Z","stars":22,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Demonstrator project for noise reduction on speech audio data using machine learning. This project tries to use the same technique as described in this paper - A Fully Convolutional Neural Network for Speech Enhancement. Here, the authors propose the Cascaded Redundant Convolutional Encoder-Decoder Network.","In contrast to classical autoencoders a Redundant Convolutional Encoder-Decoder (R-CED) network is used that encodes the features into higher dimension along the encoder an achieves compression along the decoder. The number of filters are kept symmetric: at the encoder, the number of filters are gradually increased, and at the decoder, the number of filters are gradually decreased. The Cascaded Redundant Convolutional Encoder-Decoder Network (CR-CED) that is used here is a variation of this Redundant Network. It consists of repetitions of R-CED Networks which achieves better performance with…","The while procedure is also nicely described in this blog post which also refers to the mentioned paper. If you are really interested you should read this post. If I would try to describe what I have done and why, I would only repeat what is already written there (and probably much better than I can do)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/goepfert/noise_reduction/blob/master/readme.md","fingerprint":"dd24012375f868787119d3e706212cb43b0059023937edde9b8ad1a7d334ed0e","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.413Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.413Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Demonstrator project for noise reduction on speech audio data using machine learning. This project tries to use the same technique as described in this paper - A Fully Convolutional Neural Network for Speech Enhancement. Here, the authors propose the Cascaded Redundant Convolutional Encoder-Decoder Network.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/goepfert/noise_reduction/blob/master/readme.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"dd24012375f868787119d3e706212cb43b0059023937edde9b8ad1a7d334ed0e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/goepfert/noise_reduction/blob/master/readme.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.413Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-06-07T20:13:59Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/goepfert/noise_reduction/blob/master/readme.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:08:41.413Z","hash":"dd24012375f868787119d3e706212cb43b0059023937edde9b8ad1a7d334ed0e","originalBytes":3038,"storedBytes":3038,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["noise","used","convolutional","data","redundant","speech","encoder-decoder","network","audio","background","better","cascaded","filters","here","number","project","training","achieves","addition","along","brown","dataset","demo","described","done","encoder","examples","gradually","network.","pink","pretty","probably","r-ced","reduction","result","results","short","snr","some","using","what","which","white","would","achieve","already","api","authors","autoencoders","available","backgrounds","barking","based","believe","blog","built","car","card.","checkout","children","classical","clean","combined","common","compressio